course: dictionary
lesson: 4718
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so you must read the words around it to find the right one. «Bang! go the drums! The trumpeters are tooting and the motor-cars are hooting.» The drums, trumpets and cannon make a noisy parade, so hooting here means making a loud car horn sound.
explain: Clues can also come from what the author says is NOT true. «Barn owls do not hoot; they give a long hissing shriek.» The word not tells you that hoot is the long oo sound an owl makes, and that barn owls make a different sound.
explain: Hoot can also mean a laugh or a funny thing, and this is informal. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. If it does not, try another meaning.
fact: Hoot can be a verb (hoot, hoots, hooted, hooting) or a noun (a hoot, hoots).
fact: «Hoot» can mean the long oo sound of an owl, or to sound a car horn (mainly UK and Australia).
fact: «Hoot» can mean to laugh loudly, or to shout in mockery, and as a noun it means something very funny: «the film was a hoot».
fact: «Not give a hoot» is an informal phrase that means not care at all.
fact: A good check for many meanings is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The motor-cars are hooting.» What does hooting mean here? | *To sound a car horn | To eat very slowly | To dance on the grass | To cry like a baby
exercise: «Barn owls do not hoot; they give a long hissing shriek.» Which sound do barn owls NOT usually make? | A long hissing shriek | *A hoot | A song at dawn
exercise: Mia says, «I don't give a hoot what they think.» What does not give a hoot mean? | Ask for help | *Not care at all | Shout very loudly | Give a loud laugh
test: Grandad says, «The film was a hoot.» What does hoot mean? | Very cold | Very long | *Very funny | Very quiet
test: What do we call the long oo sound an owl makes? | Whistle | Shriek | Bark | *Hoot
exam: «The children began to hoot with laughter at the joke.» What does hoot mean here? | *To laugh loudly | To sound a car horn | To cry quietly | To make an owl sound
